--- the victim rows are protected: reading the table itself is denied ---
select-denied
--- a read_only table over the victim directory without READ ON FILE is denied ---
read-only-denied
not-created
--- with READ ON FILE the same statement is allowed, sharing the live directory ---
read-only-allowed
marker	secret
--- a read_only table over a missing directory needs WRITE and does not create it ---
missing-dir-denied
not-created
dir-absent
--- a writable table needs WRITE ON FILE as well ---
writable-denied
not-created
writable-allowed
--- the argument-less form has no user_files exposure and needs no grant ---
default-form-allowed
ttl-only-form-allowed
--- a short ATTACH replays stored metadata and stays loadable after a revoke ---
short-attach-allowed
--- an ATTACH carrying a full definition is checked like CREATE ---
full-attach-denied
not-created
--- a RESTORE carries a fresh definition and is checked like CREATE ---
restore-denied
not-created
restore-allowed
